{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franklesniak/PSStyleGuide/pulls/235","id":4764069000,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQkjdhM8AAAABG_XsiA","html_url":"https://github.com/franklesniak/PSStyleGuide/pull/235","diff_url":"https://github.com/franklesniak/PSStyleGuide/pull/235.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/franklesniak/PSStyleGuide/pull/235.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/franklesniak/PSStyleGuide/issues/235","number":235,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Carry shared validation and review setup fixes back to PowerShell","user":{"login":"franklesniak","id":11204406,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjA0NDA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11204406?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/franklesniak","html_url":"https://github.com/franklesniak","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/franklesniak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/franklesniak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/franklesniak/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/franklesniak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/franklesniak/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/franklesniak/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/franklesniak/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/franklesniak/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/franklesniak/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Problem and resulting behavior\r\n\r\nPowerShell's shared validation and review setup lack the fixes accepted in [TerraformStyleGuide #68](https://github.com/franklesniak/TerraformStyleGuide/pull/68). This ten-file carryback brings those fixes into PowerShell while preserving its package identities, P1 fixture, guide names and blank-line checks.\r\n\r\nMarkdown checks still run a fresh native parser on every call. The checker can reuse at most eight bounded structural snapshots when the complete input and helper identities match. Results remain deep copies. Fresh structural conversion uses the source-checked compiled helper with the existing strict byte, depth, duplicate-name, type and schema checks. Reserved PowerShell member names retain the whole-document conversion path; generic JSON callers keep their existing behavior.\r\n\r\nThe SelfTest corrects metadata date-target selection and literal-path private clock handling, including date changes and cleanup failures. Artifact parsing declares its actual byte-array output. CI proof fixtures resolve Git through required PowerShell 7 and preserve native failure results.\r\n\r\nThe dedicated Copilot workflow retains verified acquisition, runtime admission, locked installation, hooks and the final immutable-input guard. It omits the aggregate validation step; ordinary coding setup and CI retain full validation. The instruction validator checks the optional dedicated workflow in current, staged and revision inputs. The behavior job uses a 59-minute job limit and a 45-minute test-step limit.\r\n\r\nThe workflow dependency lock selects KaTeX 0.18.2 through an exact-parent override under `micromark-extension-math@3.1.0`. The maintenance note records the parent's range exception, required caller compatibility and removal condition.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- One locked installation and both installed dependency graphs passed.\r\n- Linux: all 600 Node assertions passed with zero failures, cancellations, skips or todos; all 11 validation hooks passed, including the full instruction mutation SelfTest.\r\n- Windows PowerShell 7.6.5: parser and PSScriptAnalyzer checks on all three changed PowerShell files reported no findings. Artifact output controls, strict conversion and reuse, actual setup-reader controls, four CI helper tests, patched dependency callers and PowerShell blank-line semantics passed.\r\n- All five actual accepted-base/committed-head modes passed, including the genuine October 6 UTC metadata finalization check. Proposed-policy results remain diagnostics and do not replace accepted-policy authority.\r\n- The ordinary current audit checked both installed dependency roots and returned CLEAN with no findings, accepted packages or unused exceptions. Native main matched the audit authority before and after the audit.\r\n- Normal commit hooks passed. Source, dependency and Git input guards remained unchanged during validation; all owned command jobs and containers ended empty or absent.\r\n\r\nLocal validation combines explicitly verified results from multiple runs. Earlier runners stopped on cleanup policy, cache placement or result-reader faults. Their failed records remain preserved. Completed assertions were reused, and only missing groups were run. The Node-only result judgment requires the direct 600-test success plus exact owned terminal collection and unchanged inputs; 54 positive and negative controls passed. The causes of three historical adopted-child statuses remain unknown. Other stages retain the strict zero-exit cleanup rule.\r\n\r\n## Remaining acceptance\r\n\r\nThe common code matches the accepted Terraform source with finite repository and language substitutions. The reverse comparison must use the actual landed commits. Both current remote reviews and all current CI must pass before normal merge; no failed or cancelled CI exception applies.\r\n\r\nA legitimate Copilot service run must separately prove that it selects the dedicated setup, retains the final guard and completes successfully. An ordinary workflow run alone does not prove service activation. That proof and the final reverse comparison remain required for paired acceptance.\r\n","created_at":"2026-10-06T20:08:12Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T20:08:22Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"4bea7763920c0562e5f83c62b788b97436e5938c","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"co